   "issue": "`hc : \u2200 \u2983i j\u2984, G.Adj i j \u2192 c j = -c i` requires the sign condition on every edge, but the proof uses it only once, as `hc hadj` with `hadj : G.Adj j i`. On a graph with an odd cycle this forces `2 * c = 0`, so outside characteristic two no unit family qualifies and the lemma is unusable even for edges where the local condition holds.",
